  "query_preview": "/Wednesday through Saturday/...\nAfter a low pressure system advects into the northern Plains by the \nmiddle of the week, weak large scale troughing will remain across \nthe eastern Pacific/West Coast through the end of the week. By the \nend of the week, the high pressure system over TX will try to \nretrograde over NM/AZ, but it will be battling the large scale \ntroughing over the West. Ensembles show PWATs staying around 1.0-\n1.3\" across southern AZ through the end of the week. As a result, \nNBM/WPC PoPs for the end of the week continue to show 30-50% across \nthe higher terrain of southern Gila County and 10-20% across the \nsouth-central AZ lower deserts.\n\nTemperatures this week will remain largely unchanged, but are \nexpected to dip a couple degrees midweek as the low pressure system \nmoves north of our area causing H5 heights to dip to around 582-585 \ndm. Regardless, afternoon highs will generally be in the upper 90s \nto low 100s across the lower deserts, and in the upper 80s to mid \n90s across the higher terrain. Morning lows will generally be in the \n70s to to low 80s across the lower deserts, and in the 60s across \nthe higher terrain areas. Morning lows should start to creep up by \nthe end of the week (more morning lows in the low 80s across the \nlower deserts). As a result, widespread minor HeatRisk will continue \nthrough the first half of the week with moderate HeatRisk returning \nto the lower deserts for the latter half of the week.",
